issue_context.body:
In exploring some AuthZ ideas/patterns using the new `WebApplicationBuilder.Authentication` property and relying on its behavior of automatically registering the AuthN and AuthZ middleware in the app, some puzzling behavior was observed.

In the following application, requests to `/swagger` are allowed, despite a fallback policy being set that requires authenticated users. Requests to the defined endpoints also show that the inline middleware is actually running before a 401 response is returned, which is unexpected as the implicitly added AuthZ middleware should have run before any middleware/endpoints defined in the app. The inline middleware does not run for requests to "/swagger" interestingly, suggesting that Swagger is possibly adding itself to the pipeline in a way that is exacerbating the behavior here.

Uncommenting the explicit `app.UseAuthorization()` line makes things run more like would be expected, with no requests getting through that stage to Swagger, the inline middleware, etc.

```c#
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization;
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi;

var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);

builder.Authentication.AddJwtBearer(); // <-- this will implicitly add AuthN/AuthZ middleware

builder.Services.AddAuthorization(authzOptions =>
    {
        var policy = new AuthorizationPolicyBuilder()
            .RequireAuthenticatedUser()
            .Build();
        authzOptions.DefaultPolicy = policy;
        authzOptions.FallbackPolicy = policy;
    });

builder.Services.AddEndpointsApiExplorer();
builder.Services.AddSwaggerGen();

var app = builder.Build();

//app.UseAuthorization();

if (app.Environment.IsDevelopment())
{
    app.UseSwagger();
    app.UseSwaggerUI();
}

app.UseHttpsRedirection();

app.Use((ctx, next) =>
{
    Console.WriteLine($"Inline middleware ran. Current endpoint is '{ctx.GetEndpoint()?.DisplayName}'");
    return next();
});

app.MapGet("/", (HttpContext ctx) =>
{
    Console.WriteLine($"Route handler ran. Current endpoint is '{ctx.GetEndpoint()?.DisplayName}'");
    return "Site root";
});
app.MapGet("/hello", (HttpContext ctx) =>
{
    Console.WriteLine($"Route handler ran. Current endpoint is '{ctx.GetEndpoint()?.DisplayName}'");
    return "Hello, World!";
});

app.Run();
```
